vary. But the one detail that almost never varies, the thing that seems to make an asylum story and asylum story, is that the asylum is nearly always abandoned. The former Buffalo State Asylum for the Insane is an imposing stone structure on the north side of Buffalo, New York. It's nearly 150 years old, and its resident historian Corey Fabian Barrett recently took me inside.
