Today, there are more than a hundred abandoned asylum in the United States. Many of them not all that different from Buffalo State. It's one of the reasons we're also familiar with the idea of the big empty asylum in the woods. Few, however, stopped to wonder where all these structures came from. But in fact, the massive building, the impressive grounds, the fine materials, all of this was part of a treatment regimen developed by a singular Philadelphia doctor, a physician who was obsessed with architecture, and how it could be harnessed therapeutically to cure those who'd gone insane. Dr. Thomas Story Kirkbride.
今天，美国有超过一百座废弃的精神病院。其中许多与布法罗州立精神病院相差无几。这也是我们对树林中那座巨大空旷的精神病院的概念如此熟悉的原因之一。然而，很少有人停下来思考这些建筑从何而来。事实上，这些宏伟的建筑、令人印象深刻的场地、精美的材料，所有这些都是由一位独特的费城医生制定的治疗方案的一部分，这位医生痴迷于建筑，以及如何利用建筑进行治疗，以治愈那些精神失常的人。他就是托马斯·斯托里·柯克布赖德医生。

