As part of a push to get patients out of that prison-like basement, the hospital had already commissioned a brighter, more spacious building in the countryside. But Kirkbride came to believe that even this wasn't enough. Specifically, he wished an asylum superintendent like him, who actually treated insanity, had been consulted when the building had been designed. So a few years later, when he was finally given the opportunity to construct his own facility for the hospital, Kirkbride began to experiment.
作为将病人从那种监狱般的地下室中解救出来的一部分，医院已经委托在乡村建造一座更明亮、更宽敞的建筑。但柯克布赖德开始认为这还不够。具体来说，他希望在设计建筑时，能咨询像他这样真正治疗精神失常的精神病院院长。因此，几年后，当他终于有机会为医院建造自己的设施时，柯克布赖德开始进行实验。

