00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:42.000
kind of slowly slopes down, then you put the wall in the trench, and then you build it back up on the other side. That way it still wouldn't be possible for a patient to escape, or the word they used was ilope. It's not possible for a patient to ilope, but you can't see a big looming giant wall from inside the hospital. But the most striking aspect of Kirkbride's plan for this asylum-slash hospital of the future wasn't the windows or the fences or the plumbing. It was the building's shape. A shallow V shape like a row of birds in flight. The V consisted of two diverging series of wards or pavilions.
新来的病人会到达V形中心的一栋行政大楼。从那里开始，病人首先按性别隔离，男性去一侧，女性去另一侧。然后他们会根据四种不同的需求水平按病情进行隔离。科里·法比安·巴雷特说，需要最多护理的病人会被安置在离中心最远的展馆里，这意味着随着病情好转，你实际上会向出口移动。所以这种乐观的哲学是，你刚来时状况很糟糕，

