New arrivals would arrive at the administrative building in the center of the V. From there, patients would be first segregated by gender, men going to one side, women to the other. They would then be segregated by condition, according to four distinct levels of need. Cory Fabian Barrett says that patients requiring the most care would be kept in the pavilions furthest from the center, which meant that as you improved, you'd literally move towards the exit. So the kind of optimistic philosophy there is you'd show up in the, you'd in terrible shape,
你需要很多帮助，你被送到第五栋楼。建筑和柯克布赖德计划的魔力治愈能力，加上保持活跃，会让你好转一点，然后你会去四号楼，接着是三号、二号、一号，然后你就会走出前门。由于每个展馆都比前一个稍微向后退缩，护理人员可以轻松打开四面的窗户，有助于通风。各部分之间狭窄的接触点也防止了火灾，

