fire, making it easier to seal off any one part of the facility from the others. Nature itself was thought to be curative, and so Kirkbride called for the asylum to be surrounded by parkland. That meant as you walked down the building's tiered corridors with their tall ceilings, in almost every direction you turned, you would see towering landscapes of greenery and sky. The idea was for the asylum to feel like a Victorian home, and each word was supposed to be structured like an ideal Victorian family unit. So they all do everything together.
医生在桌子尽头和他们一起用餐，以塑造理想的维多利亚式父亲形象。女管家在桌子的另一端，是母亲，他们都表现得像一家人。如果这个场景让你觉得有点家长作风，那在当时并不罕见。整个道德改革运动正围绕着社会有义务为不幸者提供照顾的理念而建立。就像父亲应该供养他的孩子一样。最著名的改革者之一是一位来自马萨诸塞州的老师，

