from Massachusetts, named Dorthia Dix. Dix toured the country, counting and writing reports on the condition of what she called the insane poor. She wrote powerful speeches she'd then have men deliver on her behalf. As a woman, she was barred from speaking herself to state legislatures. Nonetheless, one by one, she got 20 states to fund public assilums.
