And so they were paid for with taxpayers' dollars. And this was a time when American states didn't pay for much of anything. They barely paid for roads. Kirkbride and Dix corresponded frequently, allies in the battle to fund assilums. He even included a section in his book addressed to the same officials' dicks would have been lobbying. He reminded them that anyone including them could go insane. It didn't matter their race or creed or class. Kirkbride called insanity the great leveler.
